-- title:
--   Newform behind an 𝒪-point, with Tₚ adjoined
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero, complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime whose image in $\mathcal O$ lies in the maximal ideal, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers containing $p$, and let $N$ be a nonzero level with $p \nmid N$ all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$; assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ have an integral structure, i.e. the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathbb Z$-module generated by the forms with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is everything. Let $\theta_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the anemic Hecke algebra $\mathbb T = \mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,N\,2\,S$ — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$, and let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localisation $\mathrm{heckeLocal}\,N\,S\,\mathcal O\,\theta_0$ of the base-changed Hecke algebra at the prime $\ker\theta_0$ to $\mathcal O$. Then there exist a nonzero $M$ dividing $N$, a cusp form $g$ of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform in the sense of the multiplicativity and recursion relations for its $q$-coefficients, whose eigensystem is not already matched at the good primes by a normalised eigenform of any proper divisor level of $M$), a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,M\,2\,(S \setminus \{p\})$ to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell) = a_\ell(g)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S \setminus \{p\}$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the image of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O$ such that $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) = \pi_{T_0}(\pi(T_\ell))$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, where $\pi$ is the canonical map from $\mathbb T$ into the localisation.
--
--   This is the step producing the weight-two newform, its complex eigencharacter and an $\mathcal O$-valued embedding of the generated coefficient ring, attached to an $\mathcal O$-valued point of the local Hecke algebra; unlike the version of the statement for the Hecke algebra away from $S$, the level-$M$ character here is defined on the algebra away from $S \setminus \{p\}$, so that $T_p$ is one of its generators. It feeds the analysis of the point at $p$, in particular the statements about ordinarity and about the unit root attached to such a point.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeLocal_exists_isNewform_chig_iota_of_point_of_not_dvd.lean

